1
00:00:05,166 --> 00:00:08,041
This is a trap.

2
00:00:08,041 --> 00:00:10,083
It was snapped intentionally.

3
00:00:10,083 --> 00:00:13,125
You knew we wouldn't fail to notice it,

4
00:00:13,125 --> 00:00:17,041
so marching into the forest must
be exactly what you want us to do.

5
00:00:17,083 --> 00:00:19,166
I've seen through your ploy!

6
00:00:19,166 --> 00:00:22,125
Why don't you give it up and come on out?

7
00:00:25,125 --> 00:00:28,208
The Fly Swordsman, a subordinate
who appears in the legend

8
00:00:28,208 --> 00:00:30,125
of the Lord of the Flies, hmm?

9
00:00:31,083 --> 00:00:33,083
I don't know who you are,

10
00:00:33,083 --> 00:00:36,208
but if you hand over the leopardman
and the girl, I'll spare your life.

11
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:40,166
Better yet, I'll even welcome
you into the ranks of Ashint.

12
00:00:40,208 --> 00:00:43,208
You seem to be a rather skilled warrior.

13
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:45,166
And if I refuse?

14
00:00:45,166 --> 00:00:48,041
Then I'll bestow suffering with my curses.

15
00:00:48,083 --> 00:00:50,166
Suffering so great you'll rue being alive.

16
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:54,041
Even the Five Dragoons could
not fend off our curses.

17
00:00:54,208 --> 00:00:56,125
You claim to be the ones who slew them?

18
00:00:56,125 --> 00:01:00,125
Yes. Even Humanity's Strongest
was powerless before our curses.

19
00:01:01,208 --> 00:01:05,000
Promise me you'll guarantee
Eve and that girl's safety.

20
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:08,000
You have my word on the matter.

21
00:01:08,041 --> 00:01:10,166
Very well. Then I'll lead you to them.

22
00:01:11,041 --> 00:01:13,166
Everyone, please follow me.

23
00:01:14,083 --> 00:01:15,208
I see.

24
00:01:15,208 --> 00:01:17,125
Halt, all of you.

25
00:01:18,166 --> 00:01:22,083
You have no intention
of simply handing them over.

26
00:01:22,125 --> 00:01:23,166
Isn't that right?

27
00:02:57,125 --> 00:02:58,166
DARK PLOT ~MISSING~
- How...?

28
00:02:58,208 --> 00:03:00,166
DARK PLOT ~MISSING~
- You wording gave you away.

29
00:03:00,208 --> 00:03:01,166
DARK PLOT ~MISSING~
- Just now, you said "everyone."

30
00:03:01,208 --> 00:03:03,125
Just now, you said "everyone."

31
00:03:03,125 --> 00:03:06,000
A few men would be plenty
to accompany you.

32
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:10,166
But you were trying to lead us
all into the woods.

33
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:14,083
Perhaps you need us in
range for something. Is that it?

34
00:03:14,166 --> 00:03:17,208
Maintain your distance
and prepare to attack, men.

35
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:21,041
I thought you were going to kill me
with your masterful curses.

36
00:03:21,041 --> 00:03:23,166
I'll let you in on a little secret.

37
00:03:23,208 --> 00:03:29,000
My Ashint soldiers here are
the successors of the assassin's guild.

38
00:03:29,041 --> 00:03:33,000
A hero from another world once declared
the guild evil and exterminated it,

39
00:03:33,041 --> 00:03:37,125
but we've taken up their line of work

40
00:03:37,125 --> 00:03:39,083
as users of curse magic.

41
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:41,208
So you use poisons?

42
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:43,125
Correct.

43
00:03:43,166 --> 00:03:46,166
Incredibly advanced ones.

44
00:03:46,166 --> 00:03:50,166
Ones that can only be synthesized via
special techniques passed down

45
00:03:50,208 --> 00:03:53,208
among the few survivors
of the assassin's guild.

46
00:03:54,041 --> 00:03:57,208
So they kill people with advanced
poison that leaves no trace.

47
00:03:58,000 --> 00:03:59,208
That's the true nature of their "curses."

48
00:04:00,041 --> 00:04:04,208
Then the tragedy of the Black
Dragon Knights fell into our lap.

49
00:04:04,208 --> 00:04:08,125
The sudden demise of the Five Dragoons
heralded as the strongest aliveâ€”

50
00:04:08,125 --> 00:04:11,083
Could only be explained by curses
beyond human understanding.

51
00:04:11,166 --> 00:04:13,208
You are wonderfully quick on the uptake.

52
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:16,208
That is why we proclaimed ourselves
the slayers of the Five Dragoons.

53
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:20,166
We decided it was the perfect opportunity
to foster belief in our curses.

54
00:04:20,208 --> 00:04:23,208
No one can prove they aren't real!

55
00:04:23,208 --> 00:04:25,166
Maybe it really was a curse!

56
00:04:25,166 --> 00:04:30,166
So long as such uncertainty remains,
we come out on top no matter what!

57
00:04:30,166 --> 00:04:34,125
In this world, without any proof,
those with the loudest claim take all!

58
00:04:34,166 --> 00:04:37,000
So what is your ultimate goal?

59
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:42,083
We're going to use Duke Zuan to carve out
a central role for us in this nation.

60
00:04:42,083 --> 00:04:44,166
All while assassinating
those who get in your way?

61
00:04:44,166 --> 00:04:45,125
Yes!

62
00:04:45,166 --> 00:04:48,166
In the end, we'll take
the country for ourselves.

63
00:04:48,166 --> 00:04:51,208
By the way, where are your other allies?

64
00:04:51,208 --> 00:04:54,083
Aside from Eve and the girl, it's just me.

65
00:04:54,125 --> 00:04:59,166
I find it hard to believe you planned
to face us all by yourself.

66
00:04:59,208 --> 00:05:01,125
Then allow me to explain.

67
00:05:10,041 --> 00:05:15,166
You see, I'm the one who survived
facing down the Five Dragoons.

68
00:05:16,041 --> 00:05:20,041
To think the Fly Swordsman is
actually the famous Seras Ashrain...

69
00:05:20,083 --> 00:05:22,208
Though it's all starting to come together.

70
00:05:22,208 --> 00:05:24,208
So, you slew the Five Dragoons?

71
00:05:25,041 --> 00:05:26,041
And if I did?

72
00:05:26,083 --> 00:05:28,041
No, it couldn't have been you.

73
00:05:28,083 --> 00:05:29,166
Why do you think that?

74
00:05:29,166 --> 00:05:31,125
It's simple.

75
00:05:31,166 --> 00:05:35,125
I don't believe you could best
Humanity's Strongest.

76
00:05:36,125 --> 00:05:41,125
This is the man set to be that
leopardman's final bloodsport opponent.

77
00:05:41,125 --> 00:05:43,083
His name's Belgar.

78
00:05:43,166 --> 00:05:45,000
And this over here

79
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:47,041
is Belgar's older brother, Varragan.

80
00:05:47,041 --> 00:05:51,000
These two are Ashint's strongest siblings.

81
00:05:51,166 --> 00:05:53,166
And what an odd twist of fate,

82
00:05:53,208 --> 00:05:57,041
for they had a younger brother named Zarash.

83
00:05:57,125 --> 00:05:58,125
That's right.

84
00:05:58,166 --> 00:06:02,166
They're the older brothers of the Fang,
who was pursuing you.

85
00:06:02,208 --> 00:06:04,000
Now what will you do,

86
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:05,083
Seras Ashrain?

87
00:06:09,083 --> 00:06:13,083
My subordinates have already
circled around behind you.

88
00:06:13,083 --> 00:06:14,208
Shocked, are you?

89
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:17,125
Indeed, we were just a decoy.

90
00:06:17,166 --> 00:06:20,125
Cloaking one's presence
and sneaking up on a target

91
00:06:20,125 --> 00:06:23,041
is an art all assassins master.

92
00:06:23,125 --> 00:06:24,208
That said...

93
00:06:24,208 --> 00:06:27,083
You have a terribly
pretty face, don't you?

94
00:06:27,083 --> 00:06:30,208
I think I'll need to take my time
granting you my personal blessing

95
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:34,208
and reforming you as a proper
devotee of the curse god.

96
00:06:35,125 --> 00:06:37,000
No matter how strong you may be,

97
00:06:37,041 --> 00:06:41,083
all are powerless before the status
ailment caused by our curse!

98
00:06:41,083 --> 00:06:43,083
This is the end for you.

99
00:06:43,083 --> 00:06:46,000
Now, bend a knee where you stand.

100
00:06:49,166 --> 00:06:51,083
Seras Ashrain,

101
00:06:51,208 --> 00:06:56,166
I shall grant you the honor
of one day bearing my child.

102
00:06:58,083 --> 00:06:59,125
Sir Tooka...

103
00:07:01,083 --> 00:07:02,083
It's your...

104
00:07:04,083 --> 00:07:07,166
OFFENSIVE FORM:
FINAL ACCELERATION
- Assault Accel.

105
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:19,166
Let me demonstrate a "curse"
you're unfamiliar with.

106
00:07:20,166 --> 00:07:21,208
Paralyze!

107
00:07:27,083 --> 00:07:30,208
Guess you didn't think I'd have
an attack with this kind of range.

108
00:07:30,208 --> 00:07:33,166
Wh-Where's our detachment?

109
00:07:34,083 --> 00:07:35,166
I already crushed them.

110
00:07:35,166 --> 00:07:38,125
All fifteen men while
you were blabbing away.

111
00:07:38,125 --> 00:07:39,125
Poison.

112
00:07:40,083 --> 00:07:43,083
You were keen enough to notice
that Eve was up to something,

113
00:07:43,083 --> 00:07:46,125
so I knew you'd catch
that intentionally broken branch

114
00:07:46,125 --> 00:07:49,166
and avoid entering the forest
for fear of a trap.

115
00:07:50,083 --> 00:07:51,166
Which is why...

116
00:07:52,083 --> 00:07:55,041
Act like you're trying to lure
them all into the forest.

117
00:07:55,125 --> 00:07:57,125
I tipped you off that something was afoot

118
00:07:57,125 --> 00:07:59,125
and had you suss it out yourself

119
00:07:59,125 --> 00:08:02,208
to make you feel in control,
confident that your judgment was sound.

120
00:08:03,125 --> 00:08:06,166
Yet that's exactly what
paralyzed your analysis,

121
00:08:06,208 --> 00:08:08,083
acting like a poison.

122
00:08:13,083 --> 00:08:16,125
It went exactly as you predicted, my liege.

123
00:08:16,208 --> 00:08:21,125
You played along with him
to buy time for us.

124
00:08:21,166 --> 00:08:26,125
His mistake was not considering
the possibility of a greater ploy.

125
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:29,208
Seras, I was right to leave him to you.

126
00:08:30,083 --> 00:08:32,083
I'm glad I was able to help.

127
00:08:32,083 --> 00:08:35,125
Could you go back and update
Eve on the situation?

128
00:08:35,125 --> 00:08:37,041
Yes. Consider it done.

129
00:08:38,083 --> 00:08:40,000
They've turned back, huh?

130
00:08:40,041 --> 00:08:43,208
My real trap would be incomplete
if the first wave didn't return.

131
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:46,041
Piggymaru, let's connect again.

132
00:08:46,208 --> 00:08:47,208
What's the matter?

133
00:08:49,125 --> 00:08:50,083
Sorry.

134
00:08:50,125 --> 00:08:53,041
I didn't even think about
the toll on you. My bad.

135
00:08:54,208 --> 00:08:57,166
So not even you can predict everything, huh?

136
00:08:57,166 --> 00:08:59,125
Allow me to aid you.

137
00:08:59,125 --> 00:09:01,166
All right. Seras, take care of Lis.

138
00:09:01,166 --> 00:09:04,083
Yes. I'm counting on you, Eve.

139
00:09:04,083 --> 00:09:05,041
Yes.

140
00:09:05,083 --> 00:09:07,166
Big Sis, don't worry about me.

141
00:09:07,166 --> 00:09:09,000
She'll be safe with Seras.

142
00:09:09,041 --> 00:09:10,000
Have no fear.

143
00:09:11,083 --> 00:09:14,208
Can you get an accurate
headcount on the first wave?

144
00:09:20,083 --> 00:09:21,083
Got it.

145
00:09:25,208 --> 00:09:27,208
We've finally found you, Eve Speed!

146
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:31,041
We'll drag your pathetic leopardman
corpse before the duke!

147
00:09:31,041 --> 00:09:33,083
Your head is mine!

148
00:09:34,083 --> 00:09:35,083
Paralyze!

149
00:09:38,208 --> 00:09:39,166
Poison!

150
00:09:40,208 --> 00:09:41,208
Tooka.

151
00:09:41,208 --> 00:09:43,125
Yeah, I know.

152
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:47,083
There's nowhere left for you to run,

153
00:09:47,083 --> 00:09:49,125
you ungrateful mockery of a human!

154
00:09:49,166 --> 00:09:51,166
You can run, but it's futile, futile, futile!

155
00:09:51,166 --> 00:09:52,166
Duke Zuan...

156
00:09:52,208 --> 00:09:54,125
Rejoice, Eve Speed.

157
00:09:54,125 --> 00:09:56,125
The duke will mount your head on a pike

158
00:09:56,125 --> 00:10:00,083
and have that girl wear garb
made from your pelt.

159
00:10:00,125 --> 00:10:02,166
You'll be together forever,
happily ever after.

160
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:06,041
And once I sell her off to a brothel,

161
00:10:06,041 --> 00:10:09,041
I'll make her wear a leopard mask
while she serves her customers!

162
00:10:09,041 --> 00:10:10,083
You're definitely scum.

163
00:10:10,125 --> 00:10:11,166
Paralyze.

164
00:10:11,208 --> 00:10:13,166
You have maxed out active targets.

165
00:10:13,208 --> 00:10:15,041
INFLICT PARALYSIS, PARALYZE
MAXIMUM TARGETS
- There's a target cap?

166
00:10:16,208 --> 00:10:17,166
Dark.

167
00:10:18,208 --> 00:10:21,041
What?! My vision is going!

168
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:28,208
Dark!

169
00:10:29,041 --> 00:10:30,041
Dark!

170
00:10:31,041 --> 00:10:32,041
My eyes!

171
00:10:43,166 --> 00:10:44,125
Eve!

172
00:10:44,166 --> 00:10:46,041
Kill anyone who turns to flee!

173
00:10:46,041 --> 00:10:47,041
Let no one escape!

174
00:10:47,041 --> 00:10:48,166
Understood!

175
00:10:56,208 --> 00:10:58,083
UNIQUE SKILL: INFLICT STATUS AILMENT/USABLE
INFLICT PARALYSIS, PARALYZE: LV 3
MAXIMUM TARGETS: 76/80

176
00:10:58,083 --> 00:11:00,125
- Die, die, die!
- Dark.

177
00:11:06,125 --> 00:11:08,125
S-Spare me!

178
00:11:09,166 --> 00:11:13,041
I won't allow any of you to run!

179
00:11:13,041 --> 00:11:16,041
Hurry up and kill that creepy man in the robe!

180
00:11:16,083 --> 00:11:18,125
You hear me?! I'm your duke!

181
00:11:18,166 --> 00:11:22,000
I will have my way with everything here!

182
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:23,083
Now kill him already!

183
00:11:23,083 --> 00:11:24,125
Damn it, damn it, damn it!

184
00:11:24,125 --> 00:11:26,041
- You bastards!
- Looks like I don't even need
Berserk to drive the duke mad.

185
00:11:26,083 --> 00:11:27,208
Looks like I don't even need
Berserk to drive the duke mad.

186
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:30,041
Tooka, I must thank you.

187
00:11:31,041 --> 00:11:32,125
Even though I'm a warrior,

188
00:11:32,125 --> 00:11:35,208
I was beginning to think I'd
had enough of battle.

189
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:40,125
But I feel delight once more
as I fight alongside you like this.

190
00:11:57,083 --> 00:11:59,125
Spare me!

191
00:11:59,125 --> 00:12:00,208
S-Stay back!

192
00:12:03,208 --> 00:12:05,041
I'll remember this!

193
00:12:05,083 --> 00:12:07,125
And I shall not let it stand!

194
00:12:07,166 --> 00:12:10,083
In the near future, I'll see
that you meet a cruel end!

195
00:12:10,083 --> 00:12:11,125
Paralyze.

196
00:12:12,083 --> 00:12:13,125
Are you stupid?

197
00:12:13,125 --> 00:12:16,166
Did you really think
we'd just acquiesce and let you go?

198
00:12:16,208 --> 00:12:18,125
Be done with him.

199
00:12:18,166 --> 00:12:23,125
If you had only sought to play me,
I might have forgiven you.

200
00:12:23,166 --> 00:12:24,125
But...

201
00:12:24,208 --> 00:12:28,000
But instead, you tried
to go after the girl too!

202
00:12:31,125 --> 00:12:32,208
Farewell.

203
00:12:47,125 --> 00:12:49,166
Looks like it's over.

204
00:12:49,166 --> 00:12:53,083
Seras, could you take Lis
and prepare to depart?

205
00:12:53,166 --> 00:12:55,000
Certainly.

206
00:12:55,041 --> 00:12:56,000
Thanks.

207
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:58,125
Also, thank you for the backup with a bow.

208
00:12:58,166 --> 00:13:01,083
I'm sorry I acted without orders.

209
00:13:01,125 --> 00:13:04,083
You're already the vice captain
of this mercenary group.

210
00:13:04,083 --> 00:13:07,083
When I'm not able to make the calls,
I leave that to you.

211
00:13:08,125 --> 00:13:10,041
You're good with that, right, Eve? Lis?

212
00:13:10,083 --> 00:13:11,083
- Indeed.
- Yes.

213
00:13:12,166 --> 00:13:15,041
Good. We didn't let anyone escape.

214
00:13:15,208 --> 00:13:17,000
Freeze.

215
00:13:17,041 --> 00:13:21,166
When inflicted on a living target, it
encases them in ridiculously strong ice.

216
00:13:21,166 --> 00:13:26,083
But this unique skill treats corpses as
objects, which can be crushed into powder.

217
00:13:26,125 --> 00:13:28,125
What are you attempting to do?

218
00:13:28,125 --> 00:13:31,166
With this skill, I can get rid
of the bodies without a trace.

219
00:13:32,041 --> 00:13:35,041
These curse magic users
claim to have slain the Five Dragoons.

220
00:13:35,041 --> 00:13:38,125
So I figure I can pin that
on them forever now.

221
00:13:39,041 --> 00:13:41,166
No one can prove that curses aren't real.

222
00:13:42,041 --> 00:13:44,041
Oh, how proudly you boasted about that.

223
00:13:44,166 --> 00:13:49,125
Now no one will ever be able
to prove you were real either!

224
00:13:54,125 --> 00:13:57,041
Ashint has vanished?!

225
00:13:57,041 --> 00:14:02,041
All that remained at the scene were the
corpses of the duke and his private army.

226
00:14:02,041 --> 00:14:05,208
Now my plan to use them
as pawns is ruined....

227
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:08,125
Moreover, how will I
explain this to the goddess?

228
00:14:08,125 --> 00:14:10,166
If this sours her mood, then...

229
00:14:10,166 --> 00:14:11,166
Find them!

230
00:14:11,208 --> 00:14:13,208
Do everything you can to find Ashint!

231
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:15,041
Understood?!

232
00:14:20,083 --> 00:14:22,000
What's the matter?

233
00:14:22,041 --> 00:14:23,166
W-Well...

234
00:14:23,166 --> 00:14:27,000
I wonder if I'll grow like you have.

235
00:14:27,041 --> 00:14:29,125
Wh-What do you mean?

236
00:14:29,125 --> 00:14:32,000
The proprietress said that
if my breasts didn't grow,

237
00:14:32,041 --> 00:14:34,000
then I wouldn't be treated as
a proper woman in the future.

238
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:35,041
- then I wouldn't be treated as
a proper woman in the future.
- That's not true.

239
00:14:35,166 --> 00:14:39,083
Everything that woman forced
upon you was wrong.

240
00:14:39,083 --> 00:14:42,000
So please forget everything she said.

241
00:14:42,083 --> 00:14:43,125
Forget everything...?

242
00:14:43,166 --> 00:14:44,125
Yes.

243
00:14:44,166 --> 00:14:49,125
From now on, you should only let the words
of those you trust take root in your heart.

244
00:14:49,166 --> 00:14:54,083
Then I'd like to let your
words take root, Miss Seras.

245
00:14:54,125 --> 00:14:58,083
In that case, I'll do my best
to make more time to chat.

246
00:14:58,166 --> 00:15:01,208
It's like I have another big sister now.

247
00:15:08,125 --> 00:15:12,125
I'll take watch, so please get some rest.

248
00:15:12,166 --> 00:15:15,041
No, my eyes are wide awake.
I doubt I could sleep.

249
00:15:15,083 --> 00:15:16,208
Shall I lend you this?

250
00:15:17,208 --> 00:15:20,166
You might slumber peacefully resting here.

251
00:15:21,041 --> 00:15:23,125
You're just as tired too, aren't you?

252
00:15:23,166 --> 00:15:24,166
If you'd like,

253
00:15:25,125 --> 00:15:26,208
I could lend you mine.

254
00:15:31,208 --> 00:15:35,041
Um, did you... mean that as a joke?

255
00:15:36,125 --> 00:15:37,166
Pardon me.

256
00:15:37,208 --> 00:15:40,000
Stuff like this isn't so bad now and again.

257
00:15:40,041 --> 00:15:42,083
I-I'm grateful for your courtesy.

258
00:15:42,166 --> 00:15:44,208
To be honest, I've been
curious for a while now.

259
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:47,125
Would you mind...
if I touched your elven ears?

260
00:15:47,166 --> 00:15:50,125
Go right ahead if you'd like.

261
00:15:50,166 --> 00:15:51,125
Then...

262
00:15:53,125 --> 00:15:55,041
What do you think?

263
00:15:55,041 --> 00:15:57,166
It's kind of a strange sensation.

264
00:15:58,166 --> 00:16:00,208
S-Sir Tooka, that...!

265
00:16:00,208 --> 00:16:01,208
Ah, sorry.

266
00:16:02,041 --> 00:16:03,041
I-It's fine.

267
00:16:04,041 --> 00:16:06,166
This might be rude to ask,

268
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:11,125
but do you have any special
feelings toward Eve or Lis?

269
00:16:11,166 --> 00:16:12,166
Why would you think so?

270
00:16:12,166 --> 00:16:16,083
The way you interact with them feels gentle.

271
00:16:16,083 --> 00:16:17,208
Like it does with me.

272
00:16:17,208 --> 00:16:20,125
Well, I guess it's for the same reason.

273
00:16:20,125 --> 00:16:23,041
Does she remind you of your aunt as well?

274
00:16:23,083 --> 00:16:25,083
Eve is probably more like my uncle.

275
00:16:25,166 --> 00:16:27,208
Her gender and her manner
of speech are different,

276
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:29,166
but she has the same heart.

277
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:33,166
My aunt and uncle are the only the
reason I want to return to my world.

278
00:16:33,166 --> 00:16:34,208
As for Lis...

279
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:36,000
she's like me.

280
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:37,125
Lis is?

281
00:16:37,125 --> 00:16:38,166
We were in similar situations.

282
00:16:39,041 --> 00:16:42,041
We were both abused in terrible environments.

283
00:16:42,041 --> 00:16:44,083
The key difference is our hostility.

284
00:16:44,166 --> 00:16:47,125
I'll eliminate anything that threatens me.

285
00:16:47,125 --> 00:16:49,125
Touka Mimori isn't here to save the world.

286
00:16:49,125 --> 00:16:51,208
Just to exact my own selfish revenge.

287
00:16:51,208 --> 00:16:53,083
I'm not a good person.

288
00:16:53,166 --> 00:16:55,208
If you ever want out of
this quest for vengeance,

289
00:16:55,208 --> 00:16:57,083
you're welcome to leave anytime.

290
00:16:57,125 --> 00:16:59,208
This is purely so I can get even, after all.

291
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:03,000
I have my own share of thoughts
regarding Alion's goddess,

292
00:17:03,041 --> 00:17:04,166
so I have no intention of leaving.

293
00:17:04,208 --> 00:17:08,083
Especially not after you've given me
the important role of vice captain.

294
00:17:08,125 --> 00:17:09,083
Well then...

295
00:17:09,166 --> 00:17:12,208
To repay you for going along
on this journey with me,

296
00:17:12,208 --> 00:17:14,208
I'll hear any one request you have.

297
00:17:14,208 --> 00:17:16,125
Assuming it's within my power, of course.

298
00:17:16,166 --> 00:17:17,125
Huh?

299
00:17:17,166 --> 00:17:19,041
Go ahead and give it some thought.

300
00:17:19,208 --> 00:17:21,041
I understand.

301
00:17:21,166 --> 00:17:23,041
You should get some rest.

302
00:17:24,041 --> 00:17:26,125
Good night, Sir Tooka.

303
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:27,208
Yeah.

304
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:30,000
Sleep.

305
00:17:41,125 --> 00:17:43,041
Thank you very much.

306
00:17:43,041 --> 00:17:44,125
You have good form.

307
00:17:44,166 --> 00:17:47,208
You'll probably surpass me in terms
of pure technique at some point.

308
00:17:47,208 --> 00:17:50,083
Though, please remember our promise.

309
00:17:50,125 --> 00:17:53,166
Yes. I promise not to tell
anyone about our training.

310
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:56,208
It would be difficult to get
permission from Vicius if you do.

311
00:17:57,083 --> 00:17:59,208
You will become stronger, Ayaka Sogou.

312
00:18:00,083 --> 00:18:02,083
Um, Nyantan-san,

313
00:18:02,125 --> 00:18:05,125
why did you agree to help me?

314
00:18:05,125 --> 00:18:08,041
You resemble my little sister.

315
00:18:08,166 --> 00:18:11,041
It's eat or be eaten in this world.

316
00:18:11,083 --> 00:18:15,083
Show any weakness, and you'll fall
prey to intrigue and violence in no time.

317
00:18:16,041 --> 00:18:17,083
Remember that.

318
00:18:23,083 --> 00:18:25,083
Some say it puts more
emphasis on appearance,

319
00:18:25,083 --> 00:18:26,208
but it certainly does its job.

320
00:18:26,208 --> 00:18:28,166
Are you sure about this, Lis?

321
00:18:28,208 --> 00:18:29,208
Of course!

322
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:31,208
Thank you so much, Sir Tooka!

323
00:18:32,083 --> 00:18:34,000
You don't have to force yourself.

324
00:18:34,041 --> 00:18:35,125
That's not the case at all!

325
00:18:35,125 --> 00:18:39,083
I'm happy that you bought this for me!

326
00:18:39,083 --> 00:18:40,083
Sir Tooka.

327
00:18:40,125 --> 00:18:41,083
Hmm?

328
00:18:41,125 --> 00:18:44,083
Isn't it about time we came up with
a name for our mercenary band?

329
00:18:44,208 --> 00:18:45,166
A name?

330
00:18:45,208 --> 00:18:50,166
Yes. We might need to identify ourselves
on the other side of the Land of Monsters.

331
00:18:51,083 --> 00:18:53,083
I have one idea to propose.

332
00:18:53,166 --> 00:18:56,125
What do you think of
"The Lord of the Flies' Warband"?

333
00:18:56,166 --> 00:18:59,208
It's what the army led by the
Lord of the Flies was called.

334
00:18:59,208 --> 00:19:02,000
The Lord of the Flies' Warband?

335
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:03,208
I think it's a good name.

336
00:19:03,208 --> 00:19:05,208
I-I think so too.

337
00:19:08,125 --> 00:19:09,208
It's not bad.

338
00:19:10,125 --> 00:19:13,000
All right, let's go with that.

339
00:19:20,125 --> 00:19:23,083
So this is the Land of Monsters...

340
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:24,208
What's that?

341
00:19:25,041 --> 00:19:26,083
A corrupted tree.

342
00:19:26,125 --> 00:19:29,041
They say it used be a sacred tree.

343
00:19:30,041 --> 00:19:33,125
Tooka, pour some magic into my right hand.

344
00:19:33,125 --> 00:19:34,125
Magic?

345
00:19:34,125 --> 00:19:35,208
Yes, please.

346
00:19:39,083 --> 00:19:42,208
This crest was only passed down to our
tribe's leader and their children.

347
00:19:43,083 --> 00:19:46,000
The green dot represents
our present location,

348
00:19:46,041 --> 00:19:49,208
and the red dot represents
the Witch of Taboos, or so I was taught.

349
00:19:50,041 --> 00:19:53,125
So we just need to go in the direction
that connects the two lights.

350
00:20:05,041 --> 00:20:07,083
It's not fading at all.

351
00:20:08,041 --> 00:20:10,083
I'm sure time will ease it.

352
00:20:10,083 --> 00:20:13,000
I'm sure time will fix everything.

353
00:20:13,125 --> 00:20:14,208
No, it won't.

354
00:20:14,208 --> 00:20:18,083
My thirst for vengeance against
that damn goddess isn't receding at all.

355
00:20:18,208 --> 00:20:21,083
So what if I'm a fool?
So what if it's disgraceful?

356
00:20:21,166 --> 00:20:24,125
I may be the foolish and
disgraceful Touka Mimori,

357
00:20:24,166 --> 00:20:27,083
but I will show the Goddess Vicius hell!

358
00:20:27,125 --> 00:20:30,083
The Land of Golden-Eyed Monsters
throws us in great danger,

359
00:20:30,083 --> 00:20:34,083
but at the same time,
it's packed with experience points.

360
00:20:34,083 --> 00:20:37,125
I might never catch up to the
S-Class and A-Class heroes,

361
00:20:37,166 --> 00:20:39,125
but I can close the gap between us.

362
00:20:39,166 --> 00:20:41,166
Which gives me good reason to level up.

363
00:20:42,041 --> 00:20:45,000
I'll kill and kill and kill.

364
00:20:45,041 --> 00:20:48,166
I'll annihilate everything in the
Land of Monsters and turn them into EXP!

365
00:20:49,041 --> 00:20:52,041
You've all leveled up a surprising amount.

366
00:20:52,083 --> 00:20:55,125
KIRIHARA'S GROUP
- You have my gratitude for all the
hard work you've put in thus far.

367
00:20:55,166 --> 00:20:58,166
YASU'S GROUP
- However, increasing your level only
means increasing your base stats.

368
00:20:58,166 --> 00:21:01,125
SOGOU'S GROUP
- However, increasing your level only
means increasing your base stats.

369
00:21:01,125 --> 00:21:02,125
SOGOU'S GROUP
- You all still lack skill in combat,
namely technique.

370
00:21:02,125 --> 00:21:05,208
IKUSABA'S GROUP
- You all still lack skill in combat,
namely technique.

371
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:09,000
THE TAKAO SISTERS
- So, with that in mind, I've summoned famous
figures from every nation to train you.

372
00:21:09,041 --> 00:21:12,083
So, with that in mind, I've summoned famous
figures from every nation to train you.

373
00:21:13,083 --> 00:21:14,208
THE FOUR SAINTS
- These people...

374
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:16,041
THE FOUR SAINTS
- They're all incredibly strong.

375
00:21:16,083 --> 00:21:18,125
BANEWOLF
- They're all incredibly strong.

376
00:21:21,166 --> 00:21:26,083
At this time, we've confirmed the Great Demon
Empire's forces are making a major move.

377
00:21:26,083 --> 00:21:30,083
Our next battle against the Great
Demon Empire's army will likely

378
00:21:30,083 --> 00:21:32,166
be a grand battle well
beyond our expectations.

379
00:21:32,208 --> 00:21:33,166
So,

380
00:21:33,166 --> 00:21:40,041
the heroes our Alion prides itself on,
meaning you all, will be participating.

381
00:21:48,166 --> 00:21:53,041
We must have all the heroes
continue to level up

382
00:21:53,041 --> 00:21:57,083
while they learn actual combat.

383
00:21:58,000 --> 00:21:59,208
So soon enough,

384
00:21:59,208 --> 00:22:03,166
I plan to have them head for the
Land of Golden-Eyed Monsters.

385
00:23:36,083 --> 00:23:38,000
This technology is unbelievable.

386
00:23:38,041 --> 00:23:41,125
What is this carved into the white portion?

387
00:23:43,041 --> 00:23:44,166
It's super yummy!

388
00:23:44,166 --> 00:23:47,041
I've never had anything
so delicious in my life!

389
00:23:47,041 --> 00:23:48,000
I see.

390
00:23:48,041 --> 00:23:49,208
It's good, isn't it, little Piggymaru?

391
00:23:50,000 --> 00:23:52,041
I can scarcely believe it.

392
00:23:54,125 --> 00:23:56,041
What's the matter, Seras?

393
00:23:58,041 --> 00:23:59,041
I love it.

394
00:23:59,166 --> 00:24:01,208
Oh, no, it's nothing.

395
00:24:01,208 --> 00:24:04,000
These baked sweets are very delicious.

396
00:24:10,166 --> 00:24:14,208
LAND OF THE GOLDEN-EYED MONSTERS

